    "title": "Rory McIlroy and Wife Erica Stoll Put Divorce Talk to Rest After Masters",
    "text": "It had been a challenging stretch for Rory McIlroy and wife Erica Stoll as their relationship status played out in front of the public eye. News broke in May 2024, that the couple were filing for divorce.Yet, McIlroy and Stoll have made it clear in recent months that their marriage is back on track. Back in June 2024, ESPN's Mark Schlabach reported that the couple had called off the divorce.AdvertisementStoll is back to being a regular PGA Tour events. There was no bigger stage than the Masters as Stoll was McIlroy's caddie alongside the couple's daughter Poppy for the annual Par-3 Tournament.Stoll was at Augusta National to celebrate with McIlroy as the golfer completed the Grand Slam by winning an elusive green jacket.Rory McIlroy holds the Masters championship trophy while posing for photographs with his wife, Erica Stoll, and daughter, Poppy, at the green jacket ceremony during the final round of the Masters Tournament at Augusta National Golf Club.Kyle Terada-Imagn Images (Kyle Terada-Imagn Images)McIlroy revealed that the couple celebrated the Masters win by making a trip to Northern Ireland to visit family.Pro-golfer Rory McIlroy and his wife, Erica Stoll, showed subtle PDA at the Masters Par 3 Contest almost a year after they called off their divorce. ⛳ 📸: Getty, PGA Tour pic.twitter.com/gg06ViAN8G— Page Six (@PageSix) April 10, 2025“Yeah, just to be with them, to be with Erica and Poppy and my mom and dad and to see Michael Bannon, my lifelong coach, and spend a bit more time with (caddie Harry Diamond) and his wife and just celebrate with the people that have been a part of this whole thing for my entire career, my entire life was absolutely amazing,” McIlroy explained on April 22, per NBC Sports' Rex Hoggard. AdvertisementAfter his Masters win, Rory McIlroy embraced his wife Erica Stoll in an emotional hug. McIlroy had filed for divorce from his wife, Erica Stoll, in May 2024. However, on June 11, 2024, he withdrew the petition, stating they had “resolved our differences and look forward to a new pic.twitter.com/sJiq5VMZAs— IBTimes UK (@IBTimesUK) April 15, 2025After the Masters win, McIlroy took to Instagram to reflect on finally winning at Augusta National.\"Never give up on your dreams,\" McIlroy said in an April 16, message. \"Keep coming back. Keep working hard. @themasters\"McIlroy and good friend Shane Lowry are looking to secure back-to-back titles at the Zurich Classic.Related: Rory McIlroy and Wife Erica Stoll Send Clear Message at Masters Amid Divorce Drama",
